# Qualified Python native string sequence activation patch

Status: VALIDATED, NOT ACTIVATED on the production branch by this archive.
This file replaces the earlier unrun checkpoint with the complete, locally
committed implementation, including the version and all checksum dependencies.
It is an activation patch, not a passing full-suite or release qualification.

Source base: 7943b941bf8e08192757a90ef8abbc51b9ea6345
Local implementation commit: 21af0aa2504233f24e07c56e4076bed91ab1c79d
Expected source tree after application: 9466321bcbd4d74a67af6d7879858217a253e4a0
Candidate helper SHA256: 74126b30075fa29df161a3d0fe32c2d2bff13e3fc78205ecb3a0ffb2c2766a89
Baseline helper SHA256: 0b6fad27f24421100a3f8f59235c1e4b2c676f739a22114b1613d2bf4f05a53a

The implementation preserves exact string element types from split, rsplit and
splitlines through saved methods, selected helpers, indexing, slices, loops and
simple eager comprehensions. List += operations retain source facts through
aliases and selected helper mutations. Writes and aggregate storage discard old
element proofs while preserving the allocation's native list identity.
Unknown protocols do not acquire native producer authority.

Validation performed:
- Frozen 28-source paired replay on CPython 3.14.4: acceptance 9/28 -> 22/28.
  Native text collections improve 1/16 -> 14/16; 13 partial analyses repaired.
  No accepted baseline case regressed. Exact sink sites and clean twins retained.
  Two collection-write and four pathlib positive cases remain partial.
  Five intentionally unsupported controls stay partial; three existing controls
  stay complete. These inputs were not relaxed.
- Thirty expression test methods pass on CPython 3.12.14. The same thirty plus
  the existing list/tuple augmented-assignment regression pass on CPython 3.14.4.
- Independent existing static cohort: 672 methods, 669 fully pass, five failed
  subcases across three methods. All failures reproduce on immutable baseline:
  ast.Constant(None) versus Python None context expectation; unchanged factory
  work counts 2135 > 2100 and 8435 > 8100; ordinary argparse/subprocess sources
  remain incomplete for the same generator/map/filter reasons.
  234 runtime-witness, CLI, or raw-cleanup methods were excluded and recorded.
  Final cohort receipt Git blob: b025d4605a12dec7f278921fb64eb6bc9669261b
  Paired pre-existing failure receipt: 62a3aacb34ac90e2bcf5e0b7bccb80a15a28ef11
- Sixteen module/runner JSON/SARIF checks pass using unchanged frozen sources
  and native ast-grep 0.45.3. Optional external-tool category 20 was excluded.
  The literal clean taint control still triggers the independent py.eval-exec
  pattern, so its overall public CLI exit code is 1, not 0.
- ShellCheck 0.11.0 over ubs, all modules and scripts passes; canonical pinned
  module/helper verification, SHA256SUMS verification and diff checks pass.
- Ten failed subcases first reproduced two review defects (aliased += and
  aggregate storage) before the implementation corrected them. The final
  expression suite includes their passing regressions.
- Two previously unrun authored test expectations were corrected only after
  exact baseline/candidate comparison: eval inside the loop makes its next
  consumer identity unproved; eval before the generator uses ordinary opaque
  dispatch and preserves the existing sink. Frozen acceptance inputs and
  existing quality assertions were not changed.

No analyzed acceptance or public-report fixture program was executed.
DSR was unavailable; no full DSR, full self-scan, release, tag, or performance
qualification is claimed. GitHub Actions were not used.

